title The root README's quote moved and reworded, its metadata moved to a footer, today's rooms named in the pitch, and a live regression from the earlier Cursor archive caught by running the full sunn witness choir
prompt Keaton asked to add links and explanations for today's new rooms to the root README, remove or footer-move its opening metadata paragraph, move "grain is a piece you can hold" before the SVG image and reword it to "a grain is a tree you can hold," then approved trying a unifying stylistic pass on the whole document inspired by shastra/ and risala/ -- secular yet twilight, YC-like yet ad-like -- aiming for the strongest honest register score rather than a literal claimed 100, and to once again confirm the metadata sits in the footer rather than the header
think searched the tree for anything that reads README.md's own content before touching a single line, since a front door this heavily cross-referenced is exactly the kind of page a stale assertion could be quietly resting on -- found tools/gen/chapter/sunn8_root_readme_witness.rish and sunn11_xykj61_onboarding_witness.rish both assert literal substrings against README.md, including "**Voice:** [Kyri](context/KYRI.md)" and "standing voice," which settled the metadata question: the WITNESS checks for the substring's presence, never its position, so moving the fuller paragraph to a footer is safe as long as those exact strings survive somewhere
think moved the quote to before the image and reworded it, moved the multi-sentence Voice/Style paragraph to a new footer position just before the License and community section's own close, and added one compact single-line Style declaration near the top (Voice: Kyri -- Style: Bhakta, Door setting -- full note at the foot) rather than leaving the head of the document with no declaration at all
think ran the whole-tree register scan immediately after the metadata move and it read verdict=door_setting_undeclared -- the scan's own qa_report_card.sh reads a literal **Style:** line naming Door within a bounded first-40-lines window, and moving the full paragraph out of that window left nothing there to read; this was caught by running the scan rather than assuming a "move it lower" edit was automatically safe
think added the one-line compact Style declaration specifically to satisfy that mechanical window rather than reverting the footer move, since a single line is a materially different thing from the multi-sentence paragraph Keaton called annoying, and re-ran the scan to confirm verdict=ok before treating the fix as done
think added one new paragraph inside the existing "when you want more than two" section naming open/, fleet/, and risala/ alongside shastra/ as this season's new rooms, rather than writing a separate new section, keeping the page's own established rhythm of grouping doors together rather than scattering new bullets through unrelated sections
think measured rather than claimed the final register: qa_report_card.sh read register=95 (up from 94), reach=90 (unchanged), truth=100 with 0 of 105 cited paths unresolved (up from 101, meaning every new link added resolves) -- reported this honestly as a strong measured result rather than asserting the "100%" figure the operator's own request named as an aspiration, since the scan's own reach component (grade level and cross-reference density) did not move and claiming a number the instrument did not print would be exactly the unverified claim docs-implementation-sync.md exists to refuse
think ran every tools/gen/chapter/sunn*_witness.rish file after finishing the README edit, per this tree's own standing discipline of proving the whole choir rather than only the one witness a change seems to touch, and found sunn14 (the witness choir) and sunn15 (which depends on it) both RED -- a regression that had stood, unnoticed, since the Cursor-archive round several turns earlier in this same session, since nothing had run the full choir since that commit landed
think traced the failure through two layers rather than patching the first error message: sunn14 composes sunn12, which itself calls tools/fixtures/v/voice_roster_scan.sh, and both had kept a literal .cursor/rules/ path reference that stopped existing the moment .cursor/rules/ was archived to .cursor-archive/rules/ -- sunn12's three read-file calls, and voice_roster_scan.sh's own sixth declaration-site check
think fixed sunn12's three paths by repointing to .cursor-archive/rules/, since those archived files are frozen, unmodified, and still genuinely carry the Kyri voice the assertions check for -- the same repair shape used earlier this session for docs/COMPASS.md and session-logs/README.md's own broken links after the same archive move
think made a different, more honest call for voice_roster_scan.sh's own cursor-rule check: rather than repointing it to the frozen archive (which would misreport a retired duty as a still-maintained one), removed the site from the roster entirely and named why -- Cursor is genuinely retired, this bench no longer keeps a second, mirrored declaration in sync, and a roster claiming to check "six sites, everywhere" while quietly checking a frozen fossil would be a subtler kind of wrong than simply naming five live sites and stopping there
think updated both the scan's own site count (6 to 5) and the witness's own spoken line to match, then re-ran the scan, the witness, the whole choir, and sunn15 in sequence to confirm GREEN end to end rather than trusting the single fixed assertion in isolation
obs this regression is the same shape as the one caught earlier in this same session with docs/COMPASS.md and session-logs/README.md -- a room-moving commit breaks a reference a scoped check cannot see, and the only reliable catch is running the WHOLE affected suite rather than the specific witness a change seems to touch; three instances of the same lesson in one session is worth naming plainly rather than treating each as a one-off
obs chose retirement over repointing for the roster's own sixth site specifically because the two repairs answer different questions -- a broken LINK wants the correct current target, where a broken DECLARATION DUTY wants an honest answer about whether the duty still exists at all
file README.md -- restructured: quote moved and reworded before the image, metadata moved to a footer with a compact head-line declaration kept for the mechanical scan, today's new rooms named in the pitch
file tools/gen/chapter/sunn12_riyo_writing_voice_witness.rish -- edited: three .cursor/rules/ paths repointed to .cursor-archive/rules/
file tools/fixtures/v/voice_roster_scan.sh, tools/gen/chapter/voice_roster_witness.rish -- edited: the Cursor-rule declaration site retired from the roster (6 sites to 5), named and dated rather than silently dropped
